---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Sleep Support | Dodo & Co." description="Virtual sleep support with a custom plan, daily schedule and text, phone and FaceTime check-ins. Start with a free intro call." current="support">

  <div class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="copy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Sleep support</span>
      <h1>A plan made for your baby, and support <em>every step</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">I use a gentle, intermediate check-in method and adjust it to your baby's temperament and what you're comfortable with. The goal is independent sleep and self-soothing, built on secure attachment.</p>
      <div class="ctas"><a class="btn primary" href="/get-started">Book your free intro call</a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="arch"><div class="frame"><img src="/img/alexa-hug.jpg" alt="Alexa holding her child at the ocean" style="object-position:center 30%"></div><span class="star" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="badge"><img src="/img/logo.jpg" alt=""></div></div>
  </div></div>

  <section style="padding-top:20px"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="eyebrow">Who I work with</span><h2>Is Dodo &amp; Co. a fit for your family?</h2></div>
    <div class="who"><ul>
      <li>Babies under 12 months. Around 4 months is a wonderful time to start.</li>
      <li>Families craving predictability, with timed naps and a day you can plan around.</li>
      <li>Both parents fully on board and ready to stay consistent.</li>
      <li>Stay-at-home and working parents alike, including a parent heading back to work.</li>
      <li>Families who are honest about their struggles and open to collaborating.</li>
      <li>Babies sleeping in their own crib or bassinet, or ready to move there.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div></section>

  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="eyebrow">Ways to work together</span><h2>Start with a conversation.</h2></div>
    <div class="services">
      <div class="svc"><span class="tag">Complimentary</span><h3>Intro call</h3><span class="meta">15 to 30 minutes</span><ul><li>Talk through your baby's sleep</li><li>Share your goals</li><li>Hear how I work and ask anything</li></ul><a class="btn ghost sm" href="/get-started">Book a call</a></div>
      <div class="svc feature"><span class="tag">Most families</span><h3>Virtual sleep support</h3><span class="meta">Until you feel you're in a good spot</span><ul><li>A custom sleep plan and daily schedule</li><li>Check-ins by text, phone and FaceTime</li><li>Adjustments as your baby learns</li><li>Support for nap drops and schedule changes afterward</li></ul><a class="btn primary sm" href="/get-started">Get started</a></div>
      <div class="svc"><span class="tag soon">Coming soon</span><h3>In-person overnight support</h3><span class="meta">Per night</span><ul><li>I stay with your family overnight</li><li>Coaching through each step in the moment</li><li>Ask about it on your intro call</li></ul></div>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:18px;color:var(--muted);font-size:15px">Pricing is shared on your intro call.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="eyebrow">From a Dodo &amp; Co. mama</span><h2>“I've tried everything.”</h2></div>
    <div class="snips">
      <blockquote><p>“I felt overwhelmed by all of the conflicting information and had gotten to the point where I thought, ‘Maybe this is just my life.’”</p><cite>Natalie</cite></blockquote>
      <blockquote><p>“We had been completely dependent on a pacifier, and with Alexa's guidance, we were able to successfully wean our baby from it and establish a routine that actually works for our family.”</p><cite>Natalie</cite></blockquote>
      <blockquote><p>“Having someone who could not only give me a plan, but also help me understand and trust the process, made all the difference.”</p><cite>Natalie</cite></blockquote>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:14px;color:var(--muted);font-size:14px">Every baby is different, and results vary from family to family.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="eyebrow">Questions parents ask</span><h2>Let's talk about it honestly.</h2></div>
    <div class="faq">
      <details open><summary>Will my baby cry?</summary><p>Yes, some. Babies are going to cry, because it's their only way to communicate. During sleep training, it's their way of protesting a change to their routine, not a sign that something is wrong. You'll have a clear role and can go in to reassure your baby, and I'm with you through check-ins the whole way.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is sleep training cruel?</summary><p>No. With secure attachment, it's a gift to your child. Babies thrive on consistency and predictability, and they get more restorative sleep and are happier when they're awake. Your baby learns that the crib is a safe space and that mom and dad will always come back.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What age is best?</summary><p>I work with babies under 12 months, and around 4 months is a great time to start. If your baby arrived early, I plan around their adjusted age.</p></details>
      <details><summary>My baby is too difficult. Will this work?</summary><p>I hear this a lot. Babies are more alike than people think. They're smart, they thrive on consistency, and they do great when parents stay consistent. Your plan is built around your baby's temperament.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do you work with families who co-sleep?</summary><p>My approach is built around independent sleep in your baby's own crib or bassinet, so I don't work with families who plan to keep co-sleeping. If you're co-sleeping now and ready to move your baby to their own space, I'd love to help with that.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Is sleep training right for every family?</summary><p>Sleep training isn't for everyone. Choosing to sleep train and choosing not to are both great choices, and that decision belongs to your family. I only want to work with families my approach feels right for.</p></details>
      <details><summary>You're a nurse. Is this medical advice?</summary><p>My nursing background shapes how I work, but sleep consulting is education and coaching, not medical care. Please check with your pediatrician before starting, and bring health or feeding questions to your pediatrician or a lactation consultant.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can you guarantee results?</summary><p>Every baby is different, so I can't promise a timeline. What I can promise is a plan that fits your baby, honest guidance, and support as long as you need it to feel you're in a good spot.</p></details>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="cta"><div><h2>Let's find your family's rhythm.</h2><p>The first step is a free, no-pressure intro call.</p></div><div class="ctas"><a class="btn primary" href="/get-started">Get started</a></div></div>
  </div></section>
</Layout>
